  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Shaded by reed screens, on the bends of the Treizain road, La Moune beach is the only "real" developed beach in the town of Gassin — partly private and dedicated to a sailing school (courses, private lessons, equipment rental), with a relaxed, sporty atmosphere. It lies on the Treizain road, on the Gulf of Saint-Tropez side.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Gassin tourist office (gassin.eu) and Visit Var list "animals accepted" for La Moune beach. They specify neither a leash requirement nor a possible ban period, and no municipal order was found: keep your dog on a leash and follow the signs. Gassin tourist office's FAQ adds that La Moune and Le Treizain beaches are open to dogs. Visit Var and the Ramatuelle tourist office's "Dog friendly" flyer state dogs on a leash, swimming allowed, with owners asked to pick up droppings. Note: the beach does not appear in the list of dog-friendly beaches of the Gulf of Saint-Tropez published by Grimaud Tourisme, which does cite Le Treizain. Access is free, 1 April to 31 October every day (Visit Var).</p>
      <p>The beach is on the RD 98a, on the bends of the Treizain road, on the Gulf of Saint-Tropez side. It is partly private: La Moune sailing school runs courses, private lessons and equipment rental there (phone given by the tourist office: 04 94 97 71 05). Do not let your dog run among the water-sports equipment and trainees, and keep it close when boats are launched. Gassin tourist office, in the village (20 place Léon Martel), has dog waste bags available and welcomes dogs.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is not a spot for sporty swimming far out, as the sailing school trainees sail right in front — stay close to the shore with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p><a href="/en/fiche-plage-treizain-gassin">Le Treizain beach</a> is right next door, on the same road. The hilltop village of Gassin, ranked among the "Plus Beaux Villages de France", is a few minutes away by car.</p>
